 or \"payments-service\" or \"payment-service\". Let me try a few plausible names.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150afbadf7771858647fa", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.6,\"service\":\"payment\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150afbadf777185864800", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.6,\"service\":\"payments-service\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a150afbadf777185864815", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.6,\"service\":\"payment-service\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "Those variations aren't recognized either. Let me try a few more plausible service names.", "reasoning_content": "The service name variations I tried are all unknown. The list_deployments for \"payments\" returned an empty list (executed, but no deployments). Hmm, that's odd - it returned empty deployments rather than an error. Maybe the service name is different.\n\nLet me think about what other names could be. Maybe \"payment-gateway\", \"payments-api\", \"billing\", \"checkout\", \"payments-gateway\", \"payment-processor\", \"payments-svc\", \"payments-backend\", \"payments-api\".\n\nThe list_deployments for \"payments\" returned empty deployments with EXECUTED state. That's strange - maybe the service exists but has no deployments? Or maybe the tool doesn't validate the service name for list_deployments.\n\nLet me try more variations. I should try to find the right service name. Common naming: \"payments-api\", \"payment-gateway\", \"payments-gateway\", \"billing\", \"checkout-service\", \"payments-svc\".\n\nLet me try a few more.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a150afd51673d1abb2b384", "function": {"arguments": "{\"confidence\":0.5,\"service\":\"payments-api\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_